WEBVTT

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.270
What is your goal?

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.730
This battle to determine 
the true mage, the tests...

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:22.190
If everything I'm doing now 
has been pre-determined...

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:26.430
If I've just been guided 
along to this point...

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.810
Then what is your goal?

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.380
What are you trying to make me do?

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.340
Magiaconatus...

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.160
All the world's magical power!

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:52.890
What are you...

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.180
trying to do?

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.610
So you're the one left at the end.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:13.460
Truly, you are the Princeps mage 
candidate favored by Magiaconatus.

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:18.550
Now, put that title on the line...

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.770
and fight me!

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:40.200
Cheap tricks!

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:06.730
She can pull off this many attacks 
with a one-armed ARMANOX?

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:13.570
That force...

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:21.070
I can tell...

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.750
where she'll attack from.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:25.370
Where I need to shoot.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:27.910
She's out of sight, but I can see her.

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:30.620
VIOLA KATZE is serving as my body.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:35.490
My mind...

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.880
can perceive the whole world!

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.140
That's what magical power is!

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:48.140
That's what you feel once you've become 
the mage and acquired true magical power.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.970
You can see the whole world.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.510
You can control the whole world.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:59.130
Magiaconatus is giving more 
magical power than ever...

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:00.470
to you.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:01.570
And...

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.030
to me!

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:05.710
Why?

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:07.780
To see what happens.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:10.130
To see how we use that magic,

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:12.000
and what we use it for.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.130
To find out if we are worthy 
to possess this almighty power,

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:19.760
so great that it could 
make our bodies explode.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.480
To test us!

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.390
That's why!

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:41.700
Too slow!

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:45.270
Coming in so close was your mistake!

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:47.530
I don't even need legs!

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.290
Now you can't shoot from anywhere around me!

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.680
I'm fully aware of that!

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:58.420
What are you—

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:58.920
It's no use!

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:26.880
She's here.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:20.900
For nearly a thousand years,

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:25.010
I have continued to battle in GRANBELM.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:31.060
I acted as a referee, to test the one 
who would become the Princeps mage.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.180
Do you realize how long that is?

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:38.860
How long I have prayed for the 
birth of the Princeps mage?

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:43.100
How I wished that someone would overcome me,

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:46.020
even as I tested them and 
made their hearts waver?

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:47.150
But...

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:51.570
None of you succeeded.

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:56.460
All of you came so close, 
only to fall apart in the end.

00:05:56.890 --> 00:06:01.160
The moment you witness the 
tremendous power of Magiaconatus,

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.640
you are shaken, maddened,

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:06.440
terrified to possess that power,

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.310
and finally, you break.

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:10.720
No matter how many tests I run!

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:14.170
And in the end, you all say the same thing...

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:18.410
Peace! Peace! Peace! Peace!

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:21.590
How can one who seeks power be at peace?!

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:24.860
Do you think that will help 
you become the one true mage?!

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:33.280
That's why I'm going to be the mage!

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:35.200
And I'll show you that power!

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:41.000
I'll show you what the power you all created—
what you call "magical power"—truly is!

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:50.550
Take a good look, Magiaconatus.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:55.580
See that humans are incapable 
of becoming the one true mage.

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:03.360
I will...

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:20.310
The one true mage...

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:22.650
GRANBELM...

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:24.790
Magiaconatus...

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:25.830
GRANBELM...

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:26.910
The one true mage...

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:28.240
The Princeps...

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.140
The one true mage...

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:31.720
I want to win...

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:32.470
What?

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:33.630
I want...

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:35.190
I want to win...

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:37.060
Mangetsu?

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.380
GRANBELM...

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:40.210
I want peace.

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:43.940
I sealed all magical power 
because I wanted peace.

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:46.650
Thoughts materializing 
in reaction to magic...

00:07:47.350 --> 00:07:51.460
Humans created a power that would let 
them have their way with the world,

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:54.170
then they sealed it away 
for the sake of peace.

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:56.660
That is a truly beautiful thing.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:08:02.460
It is truly beautiful that they 
have such wisdom, such heart!

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:05.450
Then why did you try to become the mage?

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:10.260
Why accept Magiaconatus' invitation 
and try to claim that power yourself?!

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:13.380
That's why Shingetsu-chan 
is trying to get rid of it!

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.190
To uphold that thousand-year-old decision!

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:16.710
You are a doll!

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:19.960
She's not a doll.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:22.990
If you say

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:27.690
that Mangetsu is a doll created 
in response to my wishes,

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:32.200
then that is the cry of my heart.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:35.030
My unwavering decision!

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:37.500
The choice I made without hesitation!

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:42.620
I will rid the world of magic.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.460
I'll become the Princeps mage

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:49.130
and get rid of all the magical 
power sealed within Magiaconatus,

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.260
for all eternity!

00:09:02.990 --> 00:09:04.140
What?!

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:40.880
What is this?

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:45.430
<i>The ARMANOX that gives 
physical form to our wishes.</i>

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:46.390
Yours and mine?

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:52.070
The doll's thoughts reacted 
to the strength of this magic.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:52.860
But...

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:56.490
This ARMANOX can do the same thing!

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:38.540
I can't move fast enough! There are too many!

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:39.700
<i>It's all right.</i>

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:47.110
Mangetsu...

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:13.700
My fairies... They're all...

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:16.730
But I had so many!

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:31.510
Not yet... I'm not done yet.

00:11:31.510 --> 00:11:34.230
There is still magic in my hands.

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:39.300
Magiaconatus is still giving me 
magic, telling me to defeat you!

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:46.010
You cannot stop me!

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:56.730
You...

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.590
The one who'll be the mage is...

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:00.590
It has to be m—

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:02.730
<i>You cannot defeat me.</i>

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:08.660
You can't... beat me!

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:11.580
You...

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:30.180
You actually think... that will be enough...

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:33.390
to rid the world of magical power?

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:38.780
Magiaconatus was drawn... to your wish.

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:43.320
That's why it gave you 
power and guided you...

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:47.720
But... you cannot get rid of it.

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:52.260
In the end, you will...

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:54.790
without a doubt...

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:56.920
betray yourself.

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:02.740
Because... you are a human.

00:13:28.610 --> 00:13:29.930
<i>It's calling.</i>

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:51.430
<i>The air is clinging to me.</i>

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:55.180
Are you really going to 
rid the world of magic?

00:13:57.240 --> 00:13:58.210
Anna...

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:02.820
Do you understand what getting 
rid of all magic would mean?

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:06.700
You still wish to test me?

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:10.940
Getting rid of all magic

00:14:10.940 --> 00:14:14.900
would mean losing all memories 
and records relating to it,

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:18.350
as if none of it ever existed.

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:25.380
What is this?

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:38.350
All that has accumulated 
for a thousand years...

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:40.910
No, even before that.

00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:48.010
You are trying to eliminate everything 
that magical power brought into existence.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:49.940
If you eliminate magic,

00:14:49.940 --> 00:14:55.830
all your memories of the battles and 
mages you've fought will be erased.

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:58.870
The very existence of all who 
vanished in those battles

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:01.290
will be negated for all eternity.

00:15:02.590 --> 00:15:03.860
I suppose so.

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:06.370
I expected that.

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:11.930
And you will bear the sin of being 
the one who eliminated all magic.

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.860
Forever and ever.

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:26.240
This is the world you would return 
to after eliminating all magic.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:36.910
With magical power gone, even your 
own existence will be uncertain.

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:43.450
That's what it means to give up 
the power you attained as a mage.

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:46.920
No one will acknowledge you.

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:49.540
You won't even be able to die.

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:55.220
Don't hesitate.

00:15:57.220 --> 00:16:02.920
You told me that I'm inside you, didn't you?

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:05.810
That I was born from you?

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:11.620
All of my dreams, my hopes, 
my words, my thoughts...

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:13.690
They're all yours.

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:18.700
The future I envisioned is yours.

00:16:45.660 --> 00:16:47.320
Are you sure about this?

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:51.730
No one <i>really</i> wishes for 
all magic to go away.

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:54.320
If that were true,

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:57.740
humans wouldn't have sealed 
it away in the first place.

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:02.160
Humans know that power will hurt others.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:05.620
I want to trust that intuition.

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:11.130
Even if magic is lost, they'll 
just create some other power.

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:12.420
Most likely.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:15.780
People are fools, after 
all. That includes me.

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:18.950
They repeat the same mistakes over and over,

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:21.630
and knowingly follow the wrong paths.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:23.410
But...

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:28.130
I believe they still know 
what it means to learn.

00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:31.560
I believe they can grow, little by little.

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:36.040
You'll be alone forever. What will you do?

00:17:38.940 --> 00:17:40.660
I'll eat pork cutlet buns.

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:46.050
And... I'll remember Mangetsu.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.960
I'll remember everyone else, too.

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:50.420
That's it?

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:53.610
I'll see the ocean. I'll climb mountains.

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:54.890
I'll see the stars.

00:17:55.310 --> 00:17:57.290
I'll sit on the edge of a lake

00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:58.660
and read a book.

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:01.600
There are many things I want to do.

00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:06.600
You won't have regrets?

00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:12.130
No.

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.480
Magiaconatus...

00:18:31.140 --> 00:18:33.720
All magical power in this world...

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:08.510
This is... my wish.

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:52.750
Hey!

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:58.460
Morning, Kibou-chan.

00:19:58.460 --> 00:19:59.910
Where's Nene-chan?

00:20:00.350 --> 00:20:02.980
She should be along any moment now.

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:04.390
Ah, there she is.

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:08.910
What? I said you didn't have to wait for me.

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:10.730
Morning, Nene-chan!

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:13.290
I think you mean "Nene-san."

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:14.880
I'm older than you.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:18.980
Using "san" for you just doesn't feel right.

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:24.660
See? Watch me! What do you think?

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:28.870
That's very good, Clare.

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:29.660
Right?

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:30.330
Yep!

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:32.560
Whoops...

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:41.550
I have to hurry.

00:20:52.260 --> 00:20:53.420
<i>Mangetsu...</i>

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:04.030
<i>At that moment, I finally realized</i>

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:08.990
<i>that you were not just a doll.</i>

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:16.980
<i>Just like children born to human mothers,</i>

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:19.820
<i>when you think and act on your own,</i>

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:23.160
<i>it gives rise to your own free will.</i>

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.690
<i>You become "you."</i>

00:21:26.530 --> 00:21:28.530
<i>It was the same for Suishou.</i>

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:32.940
<i>Magiaconatus told me in the end</i>

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:39.630
<i>that the Mangetsu I saw was not 
merely a reflection of myself.</i>

00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:43.240
<i>She was my friend.</i>

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:50.780
<i>I believe that was my final test,</i>

00:21:51.730 --> 00:21:54.710
<i>the last test Magiaconatus gave me.</i>

00:21:58.270 --> 00:22:00.080
Time to start homeroom.

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:04.890
We have a new student 
who's just transferred in.

00:22:04.890 --> 00:22:05.860
Come on in.

00:22:12.130 --> 00:22:12.850
<i>That's why...</i>

00:22:17.350 --> 00:22:18.380
<i>I...</i>

00:23:56.990 --> 00:24:00.000
<b>Thank you for watching!</b>
